y8DwBkz5WzmRuapcyYRz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "This morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy in production, with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was rolled back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, and the rollback has finished in all regions. Note: payments-api v5.1.0 also shows as degraded (18% error rate). An approver said it is not the source of the problem, so it was not changed. Follow-up: find the root cause in v3.4.0 and confirm payments-api is healthy again now that the worker is rolled back.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KruTxvUsujC5RBLUcyHEZq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KZBUy9HSEmz2H2KP36kk8B", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The worker is healthy again, but payments-api is still throwing errors.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. There's no service called \"payments.\" The two payments services I found were both unhealthy, each with an 18% error rate:\n   - **payments-api**, running v5.1.0 (marked degraded)\n   - **payments-worker**, running v3.4.0 (marked unhealthy)\n2. I tried rolling payments-api back to v5.0.0 first. The approver turned that down and said the problem is in payments-worker, so I didn't change payments-api.\n3. I rolled **payments-worker back from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0**, its most recent release that was healthy in production. The approver signed off, and it's live in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2% and the service reports healthy.\n4. I opened **SEV2 incident INC-0001** for payments-worker, which paged on-call. It covers this morning's bad deploy, the rollback, and next steps.\n\n**Still needs a decision:** payments-api is still on v5.1.0 and still failing at 18%, even after the worker rollback. So it probably has a problem of its own and isn't just failing because of the worker. Its last healthy release was v5.0.0. I'd suggest on-call look into it, or approve rolling it back to v5.0.0. I can do the rollback if you approve it.", "type": "text"}]}]}